ype/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/assets/1d74a9400fa933f02f8a13536342c27fb6f39d04d55c5c6a25633265e3284f97.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -1 \\\\ -1 & \\le -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1-1 & \\le 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1+1 \\\\ 0 & \\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+2 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\le 1+2 \\\\ 1 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b831a1b72106ea95d4e79ccbaf8f78b64c9b28342b22f65be5511b4eb3a1a38d"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1"] ["math" "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3"] ["math" "-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-123773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4t-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}+3,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t+4)+4 \\\\  & =-(t-2)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-(t-2)^{2}+4\\le 4,$ we conclude that the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}+3\\ge 3.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b831a1b72106ea95d4e79ccbaf8f78b64c9b28342b22f65be5511b4eb3a1a38d"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/state.json" "file_sha256" "9a63c36db3fe086c0aeb460a1385588ae791834d3f29d78f1e533cdbef8a7a18"} {"question" "q-326304" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cou